Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(ui):=20Concept=20B=20=E2=80=94=20Periodic?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20Contagem=20balanced=20compaction?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Makes the Periodic Contagem one-product interface substantially more
compact for counting hundreds of products, per the approved Concept B
(Balanced Compact) direction. UI-only/UI-state — no business logic,
calculation, valuation, Firestore, or workflow changes.

- Shared desktop column header (Nome/Qtd/Unid/Venda-Un/Valor) added
  above both the catalog and manual-products lists, mirroring
  InitialStockCountView.tsx's established pattern. No Custo/Un column
  (Periodic no longer collects it, per §44).
- All 9 per-row field labels now use sm:hidden, relying on the new
  header on desktop; mobile is unaffected.
- ModeAValuationControl and NewProductInfoPanel are now collapsible.
  ModeAValuationControl defaults collapsed (known/already-configured
  info) but force-expands via useEffect whenever the
  non-convertible-portion warning is active, with an always-visible
  warning indicator regardless of collapse state. NewProductInfoPanel
  always defaults expanded (required new-product configuration) and
  never auto-collapses.
- ExistingProductSummary compacted from a bordered panel to a single
  inline line; all governed data (cost basis, unit relationship)
  preserved, only chrome and a redundant product-name repeat removed.
- Explanatory prose shortened to short visible text + title tooltip
  (full original wording preserved verbatim in the tooltip) in both
  ModeAValuationControl and NewProductInfoPanel.
- Multi-portion note lightly shortened in both loops, full original
  sentence preserved in title.

Validar/Editar workflow, quantity/unit/selling-price bindings, Mode A
valuation math, product-memory resolution, and multi-portion grouping
are all unchanged and covered by tests/periodic-contagem-concept-b-
compaction.test.ts (38 new tests, suites A-L).

Also widens one pre-existing fixed-byte-distance test window in
tests/periodic-stock-existing-product-summary.test.ts (11000->13000
chars) — the added markup pushed a prior anchor-to-call-site distance
past its old cap; no assertion content changed.

Full regression: all directly-related suites pass (37+11+11+23+22+69+
24+11+38 = 246 tests). Two pre-existing failures (periodic-stock-
multi-portion-valuation, periodic-stock-shop-switch-guard) confirmed
unrelated via git stash against unmodified main. periodic-stock-
finalization is emulator-blocked in this environment (fetch failed),
not a code failure. tsc --noEmit -p apps/tenant: clean.
